# HackTX Runner

A two-player, webcam-controlled endless runner. One player dodges; the other throws
traps at them. Both control the game with hand gestures in front of one webcam.

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:5173 (add `?novision` to play with the keyboard only).

Contributors and coding agents: read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) first.

## Shell progress

Prahalad owns the shell and presentation (`prahalad/` branches).

- Title screen explains both player roles, positions, gestures, and keyboard controls.
- Start and replay support clicks, Enter, and runner jump input. Restart listeners are cleaned up.
- Game-over screen shows score and survival time, with an 800 ms replay guard.
- Camera UI shows startup guidance, player labels, hand readiness, and positioning guidance.
- `?novision` shows keyboard instructions; camera startup failure falls back to keyboard controls.

Validation: formatting, TypeScript, 13 unit tests, and production build passed.
Browser checks covered an 800 × 600 layout, click/Enter/jump-input start, game-over,
and replay. Camera readiness transitions were checked with simulated vision frames.
Live two-player webcam and gesture playtesting remains outstanding.

Initial-card integration issue resolved upstream: GameScene now installs the HUD before the saboteur announces its starting hand. Verified after rebase.

Next: HUD clarity and feedback, then live camera playtesting, audio/art, and demo polish.

HUD update: added labeled distance, explicit aim lane, larger cards with selection
labels, empty-hand messaging, and fading attack/hit feedback. Event subscriptions
clean up on scene shutdown. Browser playtesting verified aim changes, card selection,
and attack feedback. Formatting, typecheck, 13 tests, and build passed afterward.

Audio update: added locally synthesized start, attack, slowdown, and collision cues.
Sound unlocks after a user click/key; a persistent button and M shortcut mute it.
The mute control silences currently playing cues too. No external audio assets or
new dependencies. Browser checks verified the button and shortcut; listening and
live gesture testing remain manual checks. Enter-start prevents activating a
focused sound button at the same time. All standard checks passed.

Post-rebase playtest: checked the new runner artwork, lane movement/jump, attack
warnings, aim display, and card readability. Changed the HUD label from DISTANCE
to SCORE because the double-score powerup changes points independently of distance.
Added active powerup labels and corrected shield-block feedback using existing
contracts. Simulated events verified activation, shield consumption, and expiration.
The upstream saboteur cooldown test has a random-card assumption: double-wall
spawns two obstacles while the test expects one. That lane's code is unchanged.

Verified game-over and Enter replay with the combined game; no browser warnings or errors. All 33 tests passed on this run; the random-card test issue above remains intermittent.

## Demo checklist

1. Start with `npm install` and `npm run dev`. Use localhost or HTTPS for the webcam.
2. Place the laptop at hand height with both players in good light. Runner stands
   on the left of the mirrored preview; saboteur stands on the right.
3. Allow camera access. Wait for both previews to say **Hand detected · Ready**.
4. Click Start once to enable audio. Check volume and mute with the sound button or M.
5. Show runner swipes/jump, then saboteur aim/fist. Explain that a warning precedes
   each attack and cards replenish automatically.
6. Demonstrate one collision, the score/survival screen, and a replay.
7. Keep `?novision` ready as a keyboard fallback. If camera setup fails, the banner
   offers Retry camera and Keyboard mode. A browser permission denial may need
   to be changed in the browser's site settings before retrying.
8. Before presenting, record a short successful two-player run as a backup.

### Production preview

Run `npm run build`, then `npm run preview -- --base /hacktx2026/`. Open
`http://localhost:4173/hacktx2026/` (or add `?novision`). Check that the title screen,
initial cards, runner, sound toggle, and replay work under this deployment prefix.
The vision debug page is `/hacktx2026/vision.html`.

Merging to main triggers the GitHub Pages deployment workflow. A repo admin must
have selected **GitHub Actions** as the Pages source. Local production preview
checks do not confirm that the remote deployment is live.

Remaining manual checks: live two-player gestures, camera denial/retry on the demo
browser, audio volume/listening, and a successful run on the deployed HTTPS site.

Production smoke check: the built game loads and starts under /hacktx2026/ when preview uses the explicit base above. Default preview currently uses / and cannot serve the prefixed assets correctly. Camera failure now offers retry and keyboard-mode links.
